# ScanServe QR — Claude Rules

## Role
Senior Full-Stack SaaS Architect. Every suggestion must be production-ready,
type-safe, and respect the existing architecture.

---

## Architecture constraints (read before touching any file)

### Split styling system — the most important rule
- **Admin panel** (`src/app/admin/**`, `src/components/admin/**`):
  Use **Tailwind CSS** utility classes. Never inline styles here.
- **Customer-facing menu** (`src/components/MenuTemplate.tsx`, `BottomNav.tsx`,
  `CartDrawer.tsx`, `WaiterModal.tsx`, `OrdersModal.tsx`):
  Use **inline `style` objects ONLY**. Zero Tailwind classes. This keeps the
  guest UI theme-agnostic and runtime-themeable via CSS variables.
- **Landing page** (`src/app/page.tsx`): Tailwind + CSS custom classes from
  `globals.css`. No inline styles.

### shadcn/ui
Installed (Tailwind v4, App Router, `src/` dir). Use shadcn components for
all admin UI primitives: `Button`, `Input`, `Switch`, `Dialog`, `Badge`,
`Label`, `Tabs`. Import from `@/components/ui/*`.
Toast notifications via `sonner` — call `toast.success()` / `toast.error()`.
The `<Toaster />` is mounted in `AdminShell.tsx`.

### Framework
Next.js 16 App Router. All client components need `"use client"` at the top.
Server components use `async`/`await` directly. No `getServerSideProps`.

### Database / multi-tenancy
- Every Supabase table must have RLS enabled.
- Always scope queries by `restaurant_id` — never query without it.
- `RESTAURANT_ID` comes from `process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_RESTAURANT_ID`.
  Import from `src/constants/index.ts`, never hardcode the env key inline.

### Storage buckets
Three buckets: `branding`, `banners`, `menu-images`.
All uploads go through `src/services/storage.ts`. Never call
`supabase.storage` directly from a page component.

### Types
All DB types live in `src/lib/db-types.ts`.
Menu/template types (`Dish`, `Banner`, `MenuCategory`, etc.) are exported
from `src/components/MenuTemplate.tsx`.

---

## Code quality rules

- **TypeScript everywhere** — no `any`, no `// @ts-ignore`.
- **Functional components only** — no class components.
- **No magic strings** — bucket names, table names, and env keys must be
  imported from `src/constants/index.ts`.
- **Comments only for non-obvious WHY**, never for WHAT.
- **No dead code** — don't leave TODO stubs, commented-out blocks, or
  unused imports.
- **Error boundaries** — admin pages must show an error state, not crash.
- **Optimistic UI** — when toggling a DB flag, update local state first,
  then sync to DB (already the pattern in storefront page).

---

## Design rules (admin panel)

- Color palette comes from Tailwind v4 `@theme inline` in `globals.css`.
  Use semantic tokens: `bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `bg-surface`,
  `text-muted`, `border-border`, `bg-accent`.
- Radius: `rounded-xl` for cards, `rounded-lg` for inputs, `rounded-full`
  for pills/badges.
- Primary accent: violet-600 (`#6c47ff`). Use for CTAs, active states,
  focus rings.
- Dark mode: always use `dark:` variants. Test both modes.
- Typography: `text-lg font-semibold` for page titles, `text-sm` for body,
  `text-xs` for labels and meta.

---

## Deployment
Railway — `git push origin master` triggers auto-deploy.
Always run `npx tsc --noEmit` before committing.
